# Project One Get-Item Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: get-item and inventory design for M7 Project Two
#
# Review the course-provided get-item flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, SET, ADD, or similar terms.

START get_item

 # TODO 1: Identify the information the get-item process needs.
SET currentRoom = player's current room
SET roomItem = item located in the current room
SET requestedItem = ""

# TODO 2: Prompt for and receive the player's get-item command.
OUTPUT "Enter the name of the item you want to collect:"
INPUT requestedItem

# TODO 3: Validate whether the requested item is available in the current room.
IF roomItem is not empty AND requestedItem = roomItem THEN

    # TODO 4: Describe what happens when the item request is valid.
    ADD roomItem to inventory
    SET roomItem = empty
    OUTPUT "You collected the " + requestedItem
    OUTPUT "The item has been added to your inventory."

    IF number of items in inventory = 6 THEN
        OUTPUT "Congratulations! You collected all six items!"
        OUTPUT "You escaped the Haunted Mansion!"
        SET gameOver = TRUE
    END IF

ELSE

    # TODO 5: Describe what happens when the item request is invalid.
    OUTPUT "That item is not available in this room. Please try again."

END IF

# TODO 6: Return to the larger gameplay loop.
OUTPUT "Return to the main gameplay loop."

END get_item


